  "title": "Parity decision trees on the count need polynomial depth",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "Every parity decision tree solving the false-clause search of the octahedral knot sphere's NAE formula (n = 4k^2 points), hence every tree-like Res(xor) refutation, has depth at least c n^{1/8} / log n: a parity decision tree of depth d gives an F2 Nullstellensatz refutation of degree d + 3 (its leaves' indicators times the falsified clauses sum to 1), and the count needs F2 degree Omega(n^{1/8}/log n) by Beame et al.'s Omega(sqrt N) bound for the sink-counting principle, carried through linear substitution and the decision-tree reductions of COUNT-SYSTEMS-20261110-001A.",
